---
import TrustPageLayout from '../layouts/TrustPageLayout.astro';
import { AMAZON_LABEL, MARKET_LABEL, SITE_EMAIL, SITE_NAME } from '../lib/site';
---

<TrustPageLayout
	title={`About ${SITE_NAME}`}
	description={`How we research ${MARKET_LABEL} pickleball gear — catalog-backed guides, ${AMAZON_LABEL} availability, and clear buying advice.`}
	canonicalPath="/about"
>
	<p>
		{SITE_NAME} exists because buying pickleball gear online is noisy. Spec sheets contradict each other,
		“best of” lists blur into each other, and {MARKET_LABEL} shoppers often need {AMAZON_LABEL} availability.
	</p>
	<h2>Our mission</h2>
	<p>
		We publish practical, original guides for everyone who plays: beginners buying a first paddle, intermediates
		chasing spin, players protecting their joints, and competitive players refining their setup.
	</p>
	<h2>How we research</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>We map products to real buying jobs (control, power, wide feet, portable courts).</li>
		<li>We only feature products that exist in our curated catalog with live {AMAZON_LABEL} affiliate links.</li>
		<li>We prioritize clarity over hype — including when a cheaper option is the smarter buy.</li>
		<li>
			We cross-check rules and court dimensions against
			<a href="https://usapickleball.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer">USA Pickleball</a>
			resources when a guide depends on regulation standards.
		</li>
		<li>
			When we can’t verify a claim from the manufacturer listing or our catalog notes, we say so instead of
			inventing “tested” language.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<h2>Who writes this</h2>
	<p>
		Guides and news updates are written and edited by
		<a href="/authors/declan-martin">Declan Martin</a>, founder of {SITE_NAME}. Editorial standards live
		in our <a href="/editorial-policy">editorial policy</a>.
	</p>
	<h2>Independence</h2>
	<p>
		Product links may earn us a commission through affiliate programs. That never changes what we recommend or the
		price you pay. Read our
		<a href="/affiliate-disclosure">affiliate disclosure</a> for the full picture.
	</p>
	<p>
		Questions or corrections? Email
		<a href={`mailto:${SITE_EMAIL}`}>{SITE_EMAIL}</a>
		or use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
	</p>
</TrustPageLayout>
